  "chapter": 3,
  "sortOrder": 21003,
  "verseCount": 22,
  "aliases": [
    "Eccl",
    "Ecc",
    "Qoheleth"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "A time to be born, and a time to die; a time to plant, and a time to pluck up that which is planted;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "A time to kill, and a time to heal; a time to break down, and a time to build up;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "A time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "A time to cast away stones, and a time to gather stones together; a time to embrace, and a time to refrain from embracing;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "A time to get, and a time to lose; a time to keep, and a time to cast away;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "A time to rend, and a time to sew; a time to keep silence, and a time to speak;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "A time to love, and a time to hate; a time of war, and a time of peace.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "What profit hath he that worketh in that wherein he laboureth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "I have seen the travail, which God hath given to the sons of men to be exercised in it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "He hath made every thing beautiful in his time: also he hath set the world in their heart, so that no man can find out the work that God maketh from the beginning to the end.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "I know that there is no good in them, but for a man to rejoice, and to do good in his life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "And also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy the good of all his labour, it is the gift of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "I know that, whatsoever God doeth, it shall be for ever: nothing can be put to it, nor any thing taken from it: and God doeth it, that men should fear before him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "That which hath been is now; and that which is to be hath already been; and God requireth that which is past.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And moreover I saw under the sun the place of judgment, that wickedness was there; and the place of righteousness, that iniquity was there.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "I said in mine heart, God shall judge the righteous and the wicked: for there is a time there for every purpose and for every work.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "I said in mine heart concerning the estate of the sons of men, that God might manifest them, and that they might see that they themselves are beasts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "For that which befalleth the sons of men befalleth beasts; even one thing befalleth them: as the one dieth, so dieth the other; yea, they have all one breath; so that a man hath no preeminence above a beast: for all is vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "All go unto one place; all are of the dust, and all turn to dust again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Who knoweth the spirit of man that goeth upward, and the spirit of the beast that goeth downward to the earth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Wherefore I perceive that there is nothing better, than that a man should rejoice in his own works; for that is his portion: for who shall bring him to see what shall be after him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:3:22"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
